[{:db/id "49b27fdd-cc9a-5801-b180-01f4a70bc0bf" :answer/id #uuid "49b27fdd-cc9a-5801-b180-01f4a70bc0bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9{x}^{2}}{169}+\\frac{16{y}^{2}}{529}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "e0e1ae4d-133e-5ac3-84d6-bc430526f02a" :answer-field/id #uuid "e0e1ae4d-133e-5ac3-84d6-bc430526f02a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["49b27fdd-cc9a-5801-b180-01f4a70bc0bf"] :answer-field/correct "49b27fdd-cc9a-5801-b180-01f4a70bc0bf" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "1a6b38d4-7f97-5b59-aaba-751584b345ee" :question/id #uuid "1a6b38d4-7f97-5b59-aaba-751584b345ee" :question/problem "![](images/5e/5e9a8c7db3d0a811ca1dc95db8060a5488b4b9b2fb47fc08d25f1a959357626e.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=\\frac{13}{3}$ and the vertical radius has length $b=\\frac{23}{4}.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{(\\frac{13}{3})}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{(\\frac{23}{4})}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\frac{169}{9})}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\frac{529}{16})} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{9{x}^{2}}{169}+\\frac{16{y}^{2}}{529} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["e0e1ae4d-133e-5ac3-84d6-bc430526f02a"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "b3b083f8-a5ef-562c-9608-019814b62ca2" :answer/id #uuid "b3b083f8-a5ef-562c-9608-019814b62ca2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{16{x}^{2}}{625}+\\frac{9{y}^{2}}{484}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "7913aa25-1f85-5a14-8bd8-8f5d63bb6afc" :answer-field/id #