al radius has length $b=\\frac{19}{3}.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{(\\frac{10}{3})}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{(\\frac{19}{3})}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\frac{100}{9})}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\frac{361}{9})} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{9{x}^{2}}{100}+\\frac{9{y}^{2}}{361} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["34754d1c-d6cd-5f2b-ae58-2df8c449139f"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "generator" :question-generator/id #uuid "d4491310-401d-5065-a825-13199d423032" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186087840.py"} [:db/add 17592186087840 :knowledge-point/question-generator "generator"] {:db/id 17592186087840 :knowledge-point/questions ["1a6b38d4-7f97-5b59-aaba-751584b345ee" "4d9ef7fc-bb8c-57e4-a59a-c8e3d3a4c0d4" "3bbb5303-3cd6-5c7a-94a7-126cdd38904f" "f3d99764-38ad-5c62-880d-420b0ba11fa5" "77b4bcbd-934f-5219-bfb2-10a129134250"]} [:db/ensure 17592186087840 :knowledge-point/validate]]
